  "configuration_id": "config_001",
  "reason": "With no prior evidence, the most important uncertainty to reduce is whether RNA features alone are informative for this classification task, and what performance floor a simple model achieves. config_001 (rna_only, singleprofile, pca_n2000) is the simplest and most interpretable baseline: it uses a standard, well-understood linear dimensionality reduction (PCA to 2000 dims) with no complex encoding, aggregation, or fusion. Establishing this reference point first lets me (1) gauge task difficulty, (2) compare against multiprofile/aggregation variants (configs 002-003) to isolate the effect of profile aggregation, (3) compare against stronger RNA encoders (scvi, scgpt) to isolate encoder quality, and (4) later compare against image-only and multimodal configs to determine whether additional modalities add value. Starting with the simplest model avoids confounding multiple design choices and provides the cleanest anchor for all subsequent comparisons within the 10-experiment budget."
}

